      "description": "Watch Fortuna Sittard vs AZ Alkmaar highlights and goals from Eredivisie on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 22, 2026. The Eredivisie clash on August 22, 2026, between Fortuna Sittard and AZ Alkmaar offered a fascinating tactical battle from the opening whistle. As the sun set on the stadium, a series of early disciplinary decisions set the stage for an unpredictable encounter. Early Shock and Possession Mastery The match ignited in just the 5th minute when Ole Romeny of AZ Alkmaar was shown a straight red card for violent conduct. Despite the numerical disadvantage, the visitors refused to surrender their philosophy. AZ Alkmaar dominated the ball throughout the first half, racking up a massive possession share that frequently pinned Fortuna Sittard deep into their own territory, leaving the hosts struggling to find any offensive rhythm beyond goal kicks. Tactical Switches and Hornkamp's Impact At the break, the AZ Alkmaar coaching staff made decisive changes by introducing Calvin Stengs and Jizz Hornkamp . The impact was felt in the 58th minute. Calvin Stengs unleashed a powerful finish that rattled the post, but the predatory Jizz Hornkamp was perfectly positioned to tap the rebound into the open net with his right foot. This goal reflected the dominance of a ten-man team that looked more dangerous than their full-strength opponents. Sealing the Result Under Pressure Fortuna Sittard introduced creative sparks like Mohammed Ihattaren to find an equalizer, but the defensive line led by Wouter Goes remained firm. In the dying moments of the match, AZ Alkmaar struck again to end all hope for the hosts. In the 90+4th minute, Mateo Chavez found Calvin Stengs , who provided the perfect assist for Jizz Hornkamp to tap home his second of the match. With 72% possession at the final whistle, the visitors secured a remarkable victory despite their early setback."
